<chapter id="introduction">
<title>Introduction</title>
<para>
Wunjo Make is a nonlinear video editor built on the
<ulink url="https://mltframework.org">MLT</ulink> multimedia framework. It supports
multi-track timeline editing, transitions, effects and keyframes, colour correction,
audio post-production, subtitles and titling, and renders to practically any format
through <ulink url="https://ffmpeg.org">FFmpeg</ulink>.
</para>
<para>
In addition to conventional editing, Wunjo Make ships Artificial Intelligence tools:
built-in face detection that can track or hide a face on a clip, installable plugins
for speech recognition, voice cloning and content cutting, and a chat assistant that
can drive the editor directly.
</para>
</chapter>

<chapter id="documentation">
<title>Where to find the full documentation</title>
<para>
This handbook is a stub. The complete, continuously updated manual lives online:
</para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Project website: <ulink url="https://wunjo.online">wunjo.online</ulink></para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Source code and issue tracker:
<ulink url="https://github.com/wladradchenko/wunjo.wladradchenko.ru">github.com/wladradchenko/wunjo.wladradchenko.ru</ulink></para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
<para>
Please report bugs and request features through the issue tracker above.
</para>
</chapter>

<chapter id="credits">
<title>Credits and License</title>

<para>
Wunjo Make is a modified version of
<ulink url="https://kdenlive.org">Kdenlive</ulink>, the video editor developed by the
KDE community. The rebranding, the Artificial Intelligence features, the plugin
platform and the interface changes are the work of the Wunjo project; everything else
is the work of the Kdenlive authors, to whom this project owes its existence and offers
its thanks. Wunjo Make is not endorsed by, affiliated with or supported by KDE e.V. or
the Kdenlive project — please direct support requests to the Wunjo issue tracker, not
to them.
</para>

<para>
Wunjo Make also builds on the <ulink url="https://mltframework.org">MLT</ulink>
multimedia framework, <ulink url="https://ffmpeg.org">FFmpeg</ulink>, Qt and the
KDE Frameworks.
</para>

<para>
Program copyright &copy; 2024&ndash;2026 Vladislav Radchenko
